{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfunsvuR6KKDSQ3pxKH7w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"With plain `wrangler dev`, your Worker runs locally in workerd (via Miniflare), and `console.log` output goes straight to the terminal running it. You can also press `d` to open DevTools and see it there. Nothing is sent to Cloudflare's Workers Logs or traces; the `observability` settings in `wrangler.toml` only apply to deployed Workers.\n\nThe exception is `wrangler dev --remote`. There the code runs in a preview on Cloudflare's network and the logs are streamed back to your terminal.\n\nWrangler also writes its own debug logs to files under `~/.wrangler/logs`. You can control this with `WRANGLER_LOG_PATH` (where they go) and `WRANGLER_LOG` (how verbose they are).\n\nSeparately, Wrangler sends anonymous usage telemetry. You can turn it off in any of these ways:\n- Run `wrangler telemetry disable`.\n- Set `WRANGLER_SEND_METRICS=false`.\n- Add `send_metrics = false` to your config.\n\nTo stop log and trace collection for a deployed Worker, set `[observability] enabled = false` in `wrangler.toml`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2249,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2249},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e64ccad-2244-4dee-bd28-8029eb360feb","uuid":"166e484b-5c99-42b7-bbed-b7eb2e4a02e9","timestamp":"2026-10-11T04:08:04.706Z","request_id":"req_011Cfunsvf33ZNddBUGYTThC"}
